00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.640
Comparing a company directly to its closest rival on the same day earnings land reveals

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:31.500
whether outperformance stems from company-specific execution or broader sector tailwinds.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.240
Costco reported another strong quarter while Walmart showed slowing revenue growth, highlighting

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:42.860
how membership models and operational discipline can sustain momentum even when consumer spending

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.300
faces inflation pressure.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.500
Investors can implement this by pulling both companies' latest quarterly filings into

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.020
a spreadsheet, calculating year-over-year revenue and same-store sales growth side-by-side,

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.040
then checking volume on the day-of-release against the 20-day average.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:05.040
This approach worked well during the 2022 rate hike cycle, when retailers with sticky customer

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.480
bases outperformed peers by an average of 8% over the following month.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:15.700
The risk is that one-time items or accounting differences can distort the comparison, so always

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.000
read the footnotes before sizing a position.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:24.120
Canadian investors can run the same screen inside a TFSA using Questrade or Interactive

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.460
Broker's data exports.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.800
The key is to treat the comparison as a filter rather than a guarantee.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.760
Entering only when the stronger name also shows volume confirmation above its 20-day average.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.940
image. Imagine you bought Agnico Eagle Mines last week after its 18% year-to-date gain

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:47.100
caught your eye on a gold price dip. Your order fold at the open, but the position

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:53.400
size you chose determines whether a 5% drawdown feels like a routine fluctuation or a portfolio

00:02:53.400 --> 00:03:00.500
emergency. Position sizing starts with a simple rule. Never risk more than 2% of total portfolio

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:07.660
capital on any single name, which for a $100,000 account means a maximum $2,000 loss before

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.220
you exit.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:13.860
Stop losses can be fixed at a price level, trailing at a set percentage behind the high,

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.080
or mental when you commit to reviewing the position at a predetermined trigger, such as

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.380
a moving average breach.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.080
The Kelly criterion offers a mathematical way to size positions based on wind probability

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:33.800
and payoff ratio, though most retail investors simplify it to half-kelly to avoid overexposure during losing streaks.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.200
Correlation matters because two precious metals names can move together,

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:43.160
turning two separate 2% risks into a single 4% portfolio hit.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:46.100
Drawdowns tests psychology more than math,

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.720
and the habit of cutting at the invalidation level rather than hoping for a rebound

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.100
is what separates consistent operators from those who freeze.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:54.300
fees.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:00.380
The concrete misconception to avoid is treating every dip as temporary without first defining

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.660
the exact price or data point that would prove the original thesis wrong.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.580
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:14.200
Today's practice investment is a weekly hold in Agnico Eagle Mines on the TSX.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:20.060
The structure is shares, the sector is precious metals, the strategy family is valuation,

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:25.680
The thesis rests on the shares trading at a reasonable price after recent gold choppiness.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:31.420
The invalidation is a close in gold prices below the recent choppiness low that preceded

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.380
the 18% year-to-date gain.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:39.840
The target range is plus 3% to plus 7% over the 5-session window if gold stabilizes.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.920
Confidence is medium because the valuation setup is sound, but lacks volume confirmation

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.780
or sector rotation tailwinds in the current data.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.560
data. This trade demonstrates how to screen for names that have already absorbed sector

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:59.640
pressure and now sit at depressed multiples, then pair that screen with an explicit invalidation

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:05.020
level so the stop loss decision is mechanical rather than emotional. The approach forces

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:10.180
us to define the exact condition that would prove the thesis wrong before capital is committed.

